sources=[{'id':'HUG','url':'https://arxiv.org/html/2606.17054v1','sections':'5.2, E, F.2','evidence':'Existing pinned primary-source review and official code bindings read locally.','summary':'HUG separates object-relative fingertip quality and execution, uses an approximate MANO physics hand, and uses embodiment-specific robot retargeting. Those results motivate separate geometry and outcome evidence; they supply no universal native-to-Shadow tolerance.'},{'id':'TopoRetarget','url':'https://arxiv.org/html/2606.16272v1','sections':'5.1, A.3, A.4','evidence':'Primary HTML read 15 October 2026.','summary':'Reports contact-link object-relative displacement, bone alignment and penetration separately from downstream tracking. Contact links use ContactPose annotations that this project lacks. Its experiment excludes three deeply concave objects including a mug; our metrics must be labeled geometric proxies, and neither its results nor thresholds transfer as Shadow acceptance limits.'},{'id':'AnyTeleop','url':'https://arxiv.org/html/2307.04577v2','sections':'IV-C','evidence':'Primary HTML read 15 October 2026.','summary':'Optimizes human/robot hand keypoint vectors under joint limits with a hand-size scale and temporal regularization. That hand-only objective is a useful baseline structure; passing its optimization does not establish object-relative fidelity or a universal practical accuracy margin.'}]
